s to save anything useful, I should proceed carefully. I’ll check the refine skill documentation to ensure I'm following the correct process. I want to be thorough to make sure the task is handled promptly and accurately. Let's get this set up!","t":1790706066.9218607,"summary":true},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"from pathlib import Path\np=Path('/home/ubuntu/.local/share/prime-agent/releases/0.9.5-linux-x64-bc4b0ed791d1e8b3b5d6a95249a60306d9579fc0d6038e5d7d82f068d81f008d/skills/refine/SKILL.md')\nprint(p.read_text())","t":1790706066.9218607,"output":"---\nname: refine\ndescription: Trigger continual harness refinement from the Python REPL. Use when you notice a repeated failure, reusable tactic, delegation role, or behavior policy that should be persisted as a harness entry. Returns immediately; refinement runs when the current turn ends.\n---\n\n# Refine\n\nRefinement analyzes the conversation trajectory and applies small, evidence-backed\nupdates to the continual harness (prompts, memories, skills, subagent specs).\nThe implementation lives in the host (the same one behind the user's `/refine`\ncommand); this skill is the kernel-side interface to it. Call it directly from\nthe Python REPL:\n\n```python\nawait refine.status()\nawait refine.run()\nawait refine.run(\"create a memory about always checking git status before committing\")\nawait refine.run(\"promote the error-handling pattern to a global skill\", global_=True)\n```\n\n## API\n\n- `await refine.status()` — current refine state as a dict: `pending` (whether a\n  requested refine is already queued for this turn) and `in_flight` (whether a\n  refine is currently planning or applying).\n- `await refine.run(instructions=None, global_=False)` — schedule refinement.\n  Returns `{\"scheduled\": True}` immediately, or `{\"scheduled\": False, \"reason\": ...}`\n  when refinement cannot start. Optional `instructions` focus the refinement on a\n  specific observation. Set `global_=True` to target the global harness store\n  (cross-session); omit for local (session-scoped) refinement.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Refinement never runs mid-cell. A scheduled refinement runs when the current\n  turn ends; the harness applies changes and rebuilds the system prompt, then\n  resumes you automatically. Continue working normally after calling it.\n- One request per turn is enough; calling `run` again before the turn ends only\n  updates the instructions.\n- Use refinement after observing a repeated failure, a reusable tactic, a\n  repeated delegation role, or a behavior policy worth persisting. Do not\n  rewrite the whole harness when a focused memory, skill, prompt note, or\n  subagent spec is enough.\n\n"},{"type":"reasoning","text":"**Refining global memory**\n\nI need to refine my global memory with a precise note. I should call for action and then finish the required task. It seems like I might need to wait for completion, so scheduling this immediately could help. I wonder if I should call the refine.run while ensuring to finish the action afterward. It’s essential to save the request before wrapping things up. I’ll make sure to do that!","t":1790706076.8488722,"summary":true},{"type":"tool","name":"ipython","input":"await refine.run(\"Create a global memory for ARC task-b8a232b3 based on three demos and the correct solved test: grids have background plus paired vertical border segments of a distinctive marker color, one at each left/right edge and with equal height. Interior signal-color pixels occur on rows within one segment. For each signal pixel in the segment at the right edge, extend a horizontal line in its original signal color from its location rightward to just before the right border; replace the source pixel with color 4. For each such row, also map its offset within the right segment to the corresponding row in the left segment and draw the signal color from just after the left border through the right edge. Symmetrically, demos show signals within the left segment: extend toward the left border, recolor the source to 4, and draw the same relative row fully across from the opposite/right border. Preserve all else including border pixels. Evidence: demos show marker color 9/5 preserved for rays, source changed to 4; rows across paired segments map by equal relative offset. Solved test had right border rows 2-8, left rows 21-27, markers at right-segment offsets 0,1,3,5,6; extended each right and mirrored across left rows 21,22,24,26,27. Initial wrong submission forgot intermediate mapped rows; key correction is copy every signal row by segment-relative offset, not just endpoints.\", global_=True)","t":1790706076.8488722,"output":"{'scheduled': True, 'note': 'Refinement runs when the current turn ends; applied edits are appended to your context as a refinement notice and you resume automatically. Continue working normally.'}"},{"type":"event","name":"Automatic refinement","text":"Refinement complete: Created a global memory capturing the demonstrated task-b8a232b3 border-segment ray rule and its key offset-mapping correction.","t":1790706084.754244,"stored":["harness"]}],"action":{"type":"finish"}}]}